                                "sense_id": "6ddffd46-d234-394a-a857-9392d2598877",
                                "text": "Every object, whether the growth of nature or the work of man, was neat and artificial. It pleased me far better, than if the houses and gardens, and pleasure fields, had been in a nobler taste: for this nobler taste would have been mere apery."
